Z||000000||jailer||10-26-2000||07:42 PM||||Ok,I have an 84 2M4 and this is the problem.<BR>Was having great difficulty starting. The engine would crank, and eventually turn over. But had virtually no power, had to pump the accelerator just to keep it running.<BR>So new cap and rotor, plugs, wires, and a timing adjustment later, still had the same problem. Completely disconnected the MAP sensor and plugged the vacuum line that goes to the throttle body and presto! The car ran fine. So I figured I had found the problem.<BR>Spent 37 dollars and put a new sensor in, and whadda ya know, ran like crap again. Could someone please enlighten this mechanically illiterate owner as to what might be wrong?||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||10-26-2000||08:19 PM||||did you clear the codes out of the ECM? did you read the codes?<P>I should clarify this a bit. When you pulled the MAP you forced the ECM to run in an error condition. The MAP may not have been what was really wrong. The ECM ignores just about everything but the ignition and TPS when it's in an error mode.<P>Check for vacumm leaks. Check the O2 sensor, replace it if you have any doubt, same for TPS which is the only sensor with moving parts.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||jailer||10-27-2000||05:31 PM||||ogre<BR>not sure if I cleared the codes or not, not sure how that's done.<BR>the codes that came up were<BR>13,22,34,and 44<BR>I did try changing the O2 sensor, but that didn't help, as far as the TPS, how can you tell if it's working or not?<BR>Also, as far as I can tell, none of the vacuum lines are leaking, at least the ones that I could find. Are there any specifically that I should check. Thanks for the assist.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||10-27-2000||05:34 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by theogre:<BR>[B]did you clear the codes out of the ECM? did you read the codes?<P>I should clarify this a bit. When you pulled the MAP you forced the ECM to run in an error condition. The MAP may not have been what was really wrong. The ECM ignores just about everything but the ignition and TPS when it's in an error mode.<P>I had the same problem last spring. There are like 4 or 5 different map sensors. there color coded inside the electrical connector. black, blue, red, orange, and green I think. Each works slightly different so you HAVE to make sure you replace it with same color. Every GM dealer in town gave me the same one listed in their parts book. unless yours is black IT WILL NOT WORK..PERIOD ! I found the right one (orange in mine) at Autozone, they had each of them in stock. I hope you still have your old one to see what color you need,||||reg||1
